<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">XXIV Corps (United States)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1944–1948</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">XXIV Corps was a corps of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> Army formed in 1944 for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pacific-war">Pacific War</a>. It fought at Leyte in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philippines">Philippines</a> and in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-okinawa">Battle of Okinawa</a> in 1945, and under Lieutenant General <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-r-hodge">John R. Hodge</a> it occupied southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/korea">Korea</a> from September 1945, providing the forces of the American military government there until 1948.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/xxiv-corps-united-states.jpg" alt="XXIV Corps (United States)" width="130" height="151" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:XXIV_Corps_SSI.gif" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
